TOPIC 9:

I am writing to tell you about a problem with a laptop I bought from your store last Thursday. Your store is in the city center, which is quite far from my house. However, I decided to buy it because the price was good.

At first, the laptop worked very well. I used it every day to study and finish my university assignments. However, yesterday, I had a problem with it. The laptop suddenly turned off and I could not turn it on again. I tried charging it and restarting it, but it still did not work. I am very worried because I have an important assignment to finish this week.

I would like to ask your store to check and repair my laptop as soon as possible. If the laptop cannot be repaired, I hope you can give me a new one or return my money. I still have the receipt and warranty.

I hope you can help me solve this problem soon. I look forward to your reply.

TOPIC 10:

I am writing to tell you about a problem with my neighbors. I have lived in this apartment for about a year, and everything was fine before they moved in.

A new family moved into the apartment next to mine a few weeks ago. They often have parties at night, sometimes three or four times a week. They play loud music, talk loudly and invite many friends to their apartment. Because of this, I cannot sleep well, especially when I have to get up early the next morning. It is also difficult for me to study and do my homework.

I have tried to talk to them about the noise, but the situation has not changed. I do not want to have any problems with my neighbors, but I really need a quiet place to live.

Could you please talk to them and ask them to make less noise at night? I hope you can help me solve this problem soon.

Thank you for your time and understanding. I look forward to hearing from you.

TOPIC 11:

I am planning to visit Singapore for a short holiday, and I am looking for an apartment to stay in. I am writing to ask for some information about apartments for rent in your area.

I need a small apartment for two people. It should have one bedroom, a bathroom, a kitchen and free Wi-Fi. I would like to stay somewhere near the city center because I want to visit some famous places in Singapore. It would also be better if the apartment was near bus stops or train stations. I do not want to spend too much money on accommodation, so I hope to find a clean and comfortable apartment at a reasonable price.

I plan to arrive in Singapore on December 10th and stay for one week. Therefore, I need an apartment from December 10th to December 17th.

Could you please send me some information about available apartments and their prices? I would also like to know if I need to pay a deposit before booking.

Thank you for your help. I look forward to your reply.